# Line-ending policy for the nightme repo.
#
# *.go text eol=lf
#   Forces every checkout — including GitHub Actions windows
#   runners with core.autocrlf=true and any developer with
#   autocrlf=input/true — to materialize .go files with LF
#   terminators. gofmt considers CRLF-terminated .go files
#   to be unformatted (gofmt -l lists them as needing
#   reformatted, regardless of content), so a CRLF on disk
#   makes the Check gofmt CI gate fail with the WRONG root
#   cause ("file is not gofmt'd"). Pinning to LF at the git
#   layer is the only way to guarantee that what gofmt sees
#   in CI is the same bytes the author wrote.
#
#   A PR that introduces a CRLF .go file (e.g. edited via
#   Windows Notepad) will fail the Check line endings CI step
#   that sits immediately before Check gofmt — the error
#   message points at the offending file with an explicit
#   fix command, so the contributor does not have to chase a
#   red herring through gofmt.
#
# * text=auto
#   Leaves non-Go files alone — scripts, docs, .gitignore,
#   .yml, etc. can still carry platform-native endings. Only
#   .go is gated, because only .go has the "gofmt rejects
#   CRLF" problem.
*.go   text eol=lf
*      text=auto
